WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.520
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:07.690
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.030
It's merely chocolate.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.110
But it's still chocolate.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:18.790
Valentine's chocolate from you, my beloved, is more precious than gems.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.040
Let's eat together.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.750
Love Heart Chocolate.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:28.500
I wanna eat Love Meowrt Chocolate with Subaru-kyun!{I'd prefer not doing this here but}

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.590
M4 is so amazing.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.380
Huh? What do you mean?

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:36.090
The chocolate commercials that air in the run-up to Valentine's Day

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:40.180
are famous for always starring the most popular idols of the season.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:45.270
It's proof that M4 tops the male idol charts in both name and reality. {I'll just take the jisho version of this}

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.610
M4 is great!

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.360
Subaru-kun's the best!

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.400
I'm a Nozomu-kun diehard!

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.490
Asahi-kun is way too cute!

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:57.490
Doesn't Kanata-kun just draw you in?

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:03.790
Hey! Is Nijino here?

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:04.910
Yes!

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:06.790
The headmaster wants to see you.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:08.710
He does?

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:49.350
Headmaster, I've brought Nijino.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:50.770
Come in.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.610
Excuse me.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:55.900
So...

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:58.610
Nijino, how have you been lately?

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.240
I'm in top form!

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:04.160
With the S4 Selection coming up, 
I'm getting more psyched every day!

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.700
That's all I can ask for.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:10.290
By the way, have you heard of The Best Music Show?

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.540
Of course! It's a music program that pulls high ratings.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:20.170
On February 14th, Valentine's Day, 
they're going to have a three-hour special.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:23.050
They've requested that you take part.

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:28.680
Ow...

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.850
Geez, why did you push us, Ako?

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.900
You're the one who pushed me!

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.150
You guys...

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.020
What are you doing here?

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:40.860
Well, we were worried you were going to be mean to Yume again.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.410
But guess not!

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.830
I wish only for the growth of every student in the academy.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:51.910
Not once have I attempted to bring an idol down.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:55.840
The headmaster has surprisingly bad social skills, you know.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.210
Anyway, this is unbelievable!

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:02.340
The Music Show requested you specifically!

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:06.680
The program has a segment called the Anything Ranking.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:11.600
Whoever wins the viewers' vote becomes the show's next guest.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:17.230
You won the "Idol You Most Want To Receive Chocolate From" ranking.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:20.990
What kind of ranking is that?

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.570
But why me, of all people?

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.870
Isn't it because of your family's confectionery shop?

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.580
Oh, that makes sense!

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:30.120
I'm so happy!

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.620
Is that really enough to make you happy?

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:38.170
Of course! No matter the reason, those people voted for me.

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:39.750
It's the best!

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.760
You're so positive.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.930
Will you accept the offer?

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.130
I will!

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:49.390
Nijino, I have high hopes for your performance.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:51.930
Thank you, I'll do my best!

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:56.770
Yume-chan, I can't believe you get to be on the Music Show!

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:01.780
S4 is on it all the time, but you're the first one in our year to get in.{wait, is she talking about S4 in general and first-years in general, or the specific members of S4 and the specific first year?}{uh, I figured this year? Since I bet Hime made it in her first year}

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:05.660
Only Japan's best singers make it on as guests.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:09.160
And the pre-song talk segment with the host will be just as important.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:12.790
It gets broadcast nationwide, so this is your big chance!

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:13.870
Yeah!

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:19.040
I only just realized, but my eyes had always been chasing after you.{I mean it's like that but it's also}{fine}

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:20.960
I love you.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:22.920
Cut!

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:25.760
Subaru-kun, nice! That's the stuff!

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.430
Thank you very much!

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:30.300
Subaru-kun, your acting's changed.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.310
You think so?

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:36.060
I agree! My heart skipped a beat watching from way over here.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:42.440
According to my analysis, his improvements are due to a drastic change in his mental state.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:45.820
So you mean, there's a girl he likes now?

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:48.530
And now he's totally lovestruck?

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:50.570
So, what's happened?

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:53.080
Nothing.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:59.380
Speaking of which, Yume-chan was invited as a guest to The Best Music Show's special.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:03.300
So she'll be going on with us.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.960
I can't wait!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:09.930
She must be really fired up since it'll be her first time.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.850
<i>It's nothing, really.</i>

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:21.480
<i>Just...</i>

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:26.280
<i>It's just that... she intrigues me a little.</i>

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:32.200
<i>She was invited as a guest to 
The Best Music Show's special.</i>

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:42.590
How about this one? No, maybe this one.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:55.430
Yo.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.060
What's up?

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:59.440
Oh, I brought this for you.

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:00.440
What is it?

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:03.230
You're gonna be on The Best Music Show, right?

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:07.690
They're recordings of past Music Shows.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:11.410
What?

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:15.950
Thanks! I was just thinking I wanted to look at some of the old episodes.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:18.790
Thank you so, so much!

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:19.910
Sure.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:24.960
Okay! Time to study hard and think up a good way to show my appeal.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.340
Show your appeal?

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:30.340
Being on national TV is a huge opportunity.

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:34.390
I figured I should say a few things about myself for all the people who don't know me.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.600
That's not enough.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:37.520
Huh?

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:40.430
It's not that showing your appeal isn't important.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:46.150
But the most important thing is what you want to convey to the viewers, don't you think?

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:49.150
See you.

00:07:52.780 --> 00:07:55.030
Oh, there you are, Yume-chan!

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:57.700
We've got a favor to ask.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:02.040
Why are they turning out so bad?

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:05.040
They're supposed to just cool down and solidify.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:08.800
We're following the recipe to the letter, but they aren't turning out well.{yes I know}

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.420
What could it be?

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:15.050
There are little tricks to baking that you won't find in books.

00:08:15.050 --> 00:08:18.010
I'll give you a hand, so let's start over from the beginning.

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:20.560
You will? Awesome!

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.190
No wonder you're the number one 
"Idol You Most Want To Receive Chocolate From"!

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:27.820
Sorry, we know how busy you are with the Music Show.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:32.700
It's fine. The chocolate you make for Valentine's is special.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.820
True love chocolate for the person you like.

00:08:36.820 --> 00:08:39.620
Gratitude chocolate for people who look out for you.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:42.000
Friend chocolate for your friends.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:45.500
Everyone pours their feelings into their chocolate.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:47.710
Feelings?

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:50.500
I'd never turn my back on that.

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.970
Come on, lets roll up our sleeves.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:04.980
I hope this chocolate can convey my feelings.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.690
I'm sure it will!

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:13.110
<i>But the most important thing is what you want to convey to the viewers, don't you think?</i>

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:16.410
What I want to convey...

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:45.640
U-Um, Tsubasa-senpai! Please accept my chocolate!

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:48.310
Tsubasa-senpai, I'm a huge fan!

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:49.400
Thank you.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:52.020
She took it!

00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:55.320
Tsubasacchi's getting all the girls.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:56.900
She's beloved.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:01.780
That she is.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.540
Oh, Mahiru!

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:04.790
Here.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:06.620
For me?

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:09.330
I-It's not like that, okay?

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:12.290
You've helped me out a little, so I just wanted—

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.460
Mahiru!

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:16.340
That makes Onee-chan so happy!

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.300
Hey, knock it off!

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.550
Stop, Onee-chan!

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.260
They're so close.

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.310
It's getting hot out here!

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:31.060
"Dear Subaru-kyun, this is filled with my love."

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:33.110
But seriously, this thing is huge.

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:35.440
This thing is solid chocolate.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:37.440
Her love is too big.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:43.700
<i>I couldn't help it! I kept thinking of 
Subaru-kyun and it just grew and grew!</i>

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:46.830
There's no sender on here.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:51.580
Hey, whoever made me this chocolate!

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:54.420
Thank you! {sankyuu}{needs a tl note}

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:01.890
<i>Subaru-kyun said "thank you" to me!</i>

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:06.810
<i>From now on, Valentine's Day will be our "thank you" anniversary!</i>

00:11:10.190 --> 00:11:14.940
I'm sorry you had to go through the trouble of preparing me a car, Anna-sensei.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:17.150
Don't be so cold, baby.

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:20.570
You're going to be on The Best Music Show.

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:23.200
It's the academy's job to provide you with backup.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:28.200
Besides, a teacher always wants to help her students thrive.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.080
Anna-sensei!

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.330
Yume!

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.080
Yume-chan!

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:36.840
Everyone! You came to see me off?

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.300
Why wouldn't we?

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.590
Thank goodness we made it.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.890
Here, friend chocolate.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.890
I wanted to get it to you before you left.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:46.720
Thanks!

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:50.270
Do!

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:51.060
It!

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.810
Yume-chan!

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:56.820
"You can do it, Yume-chan"? Don't tell me...

00:11:56.820 --> 00:12:00.440
We made it in secret while you were busy with your lessons.

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:03.320
We'll be cheering for you, so go and nail it!

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:11.580
Time to step on it with defensive driving!

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:20.340
<i>Okay everyone, here I go.</i>

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.840
Prepare to go live!

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.930
Three! Two!

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:32.350
Good evening, viewers. 
I am your host, Makisugi Makiko.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:37.110
Welcome to The Best Music Show's three-hour Valentine special,

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.480
brought to you live from our studio.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:40.530
It started!

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.700
Where's Yume? Where is she?

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.610
She's not on yet.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.240
Let us begin right away.

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:50.120
Allow me to introduce today's guests.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:55.000
First, we have our nationally beloved idols, the boys of M4.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:05.590
Next, making her first appearance on the show, is Nijino Yume-san.

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.510
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:13.930
Oh my!

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:16.230
<i>That octopus!{wait is this what it is now? not octopus or octogirl or whatever}{situational, full ver is boiled octopus}</i>

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.110
<i>This is nothing!</i>

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.030
Safe!

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:26.030
Nijino-san, you have a remarkable sense of balance.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:32.450
Geez...

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:34.910
She had me on the edge of my seat.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:36.330
That gets me going.

00:13:36.330 --> 00:13:38.250
She's grabbed everyone's attention.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:42.130
I have a question for you, M4.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:46.090
Is it true that you receive a large amount of Valentine's chocolate?

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:48.390
Ten truckloads worth. {this is exactly the amount Soleil got too}

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:50.430
Just look at this!

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:56.020
This is all Valentine's chocolate that fans have sent M4!

00:13:56.390 --> 00:14:00.650
That is a stunning amount of chocolate. What will you do with it all?

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:02.610
Naturally, we'll eat it.

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:03.860
In its entirety?

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.530
Yep, all of it.

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:10.030
Every piece of chocolate has a fan's feelings poured into it.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:17.410
Here is M4 with their song, "Our Miracle".

00:14:17.410 --> 00:14:19.790
Subaru-kyun!

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:22.730
<i>What a reaction. It feels like the whole studio is shaking.</i>

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:28.240
<i>Come to think of it, this is the first time I've ever actually seen M4 perform.</i>

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:31.240
<i>Every single fan is smiling.</i>

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:33.820
<i>M4 is amazing!</i>

00:15:36.950 --> 00:15:42.500
Now then, here for her first visit is 
Four Star Academy's Nijino Yume-san.

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.380
Thank you for having me.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:50.010
You outshone the field in the "Idol You Most Want To Receive Chocolate From" ranking.

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:54.260
I was overjoyed. I'd like to give everyone chocolate too.

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:57.260
The chocolate from my family's shop is delicious.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:16:00.890
Please come visit us at Rainbow Confectionery!

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:06.980
What a reliable daughter your parents have.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:09.530
Do you bake chocolate often?

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:16.370
Unfortunately, I was so busy preparing for this show 
that I was unable to make my own chocolate this year.

00:16:17.080 --> 00:16:18.080
Instead...

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:20.370
I got a lot of friend chocolate!

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:24.170
They poured their warm hearts into this chocolate.

00:16:24.170 --> 00:16:26.380
It made me very happy!

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:28.000
Yume...

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:37.140
I feel very, very blessed to have such wonderful friends supporting me and fans voting for me.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:41.980
I'd like to convey my happiness to them through this song.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:53.700
<i>But the most important thing is what you want to convey to the viewers, don't you think?</i>

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:58.620
Nijino Yume, ready to go!

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:16.060
What is this Glitter?

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:18.980
That's special Grade-up Glitter!

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:23.320
It's one-of-a-kind, and made exclusively for you.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.320
Exclusively for me?!

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:29.540
With it, you'll be able to make a unique dress that's all your own.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:31.540
The S4 Selection is looking up.

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:34.540
A dress all my own!

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:37.090
I wonder how it'll be!

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.220
Hey!

00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:51.060
I'm glad I managed to get your attention.

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:54.310
That's great, but why did you come so late at night?

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:57.810
Because it's pointless if I don't do it today.

00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:01.900
I couldn't resist giving everyone chocolate, so I made it in a hurry.

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:05.070
Here, my Valentine's chocolate.

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:09.330
Um... it's friend chocolate, I guess?

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:11.200
It's not friend chocolate.

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:14.790
We're not really friends, but something more special.

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:19.290
I wrote my feelings on the chocolate, so take a look.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:20.750
O-Okay.

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:25.930
"Rival confirmed"?

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:27.090
What is this?

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:31.430
Rival chocolate! I was moved after seeing M4's performance.

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:34.560
So starting today, you're my rival!

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:39.520
Who even thinks of rival chocolate?

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:41.230
You led me on!

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:47.320
I got to be in the Music Show, and I made a new rival. Today was an amazing day!

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.570
I can't contain my excitement!

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:54.540
What is it?

00:21:58.080 --> 00:21:59.580
What was that for?

00:21:59.580 --> 00:22:04.210
Taking on M4 as your rivals? That's some guts you've got.

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:07.800
I'm going to become the first-star idol.

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:10.970
Isn't it better to have strong rivals?

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:12.600
Can't argue that.

00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:17.100
Looks like it's a race to see who can become a first-star idol first.{do we have a repeat of the "a top idol" vs "the top idol" problem going on now}{okay I'll separate them by gender}

00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:18.060
Yeah!

00:24:10.880 --> 00:24:14.800
To tell you the truth, I've been wanting to perform with you, Rola.

00:24:14.800 --> 00:24:16.600
Me too!

00:24:16.600 --> 00:24:18.180
I'll cheer you on!

00:24:18.180 --> 00:24:20.520
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.520 --> 00:24:21.980
Premonitions of Spring.

00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:24.020
Become the first-star idol!
